first heading = Release notes

--- rendered ---
<h1>Release notes</h1>
<p>The parser handles <em>emphasis</em>, <strong>strong emphasis</strong>, <code>code spans</code>,
and <a href="https://vyto.dev" title="the site">links</a>.</p>
<h2>What landed</h2>
<ul>
<li>CSV, with real quoting</li>
<li>XML, with namespaces
<ul>
<li>a pull reader</li>
<li>and a DOM</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>TOML and INI</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>First</li>
<li>Second</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>Every module is pure Vyto.
No native code at all.</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code class="language-vyto">let doc = md_parse(source);
</code></pre>
<hr>
<p>Raw &lt;b&gt;HTML&lt;/b&gt; is escaped, not forwarded.</p>

--- inline ---
<p><em>em</em> and <strong>strong</strong> and <em><strong>both</strong></em></p>
<p><code>code</code> and <code>a ` inside</code> and <code>`</code></p>
<p><a href="url">text</a> and <img src="img.png" alt="alt" title="t"> and <a href="https://auto.link">https://auto.link</a></p>
<p>a snake_case_name keeps its underscores</p>
<p>but a<em>star</em>works intraword</p>
<p>escapes: *not emphasis* and # not a heading</p>
<p>a hard break follows this<br>
and a soft one
follows this</p>

